From 27786a27cecb5f164b1cfa339521ef7865872e14 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 16:28:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(rust-rounds): carry the owner's opening take from the
 send to the essay

paulgsc/some-ui#3269. A /2 Rust Rounds week may carry an opening, and the
owner records a take of it whose ref is <week>:opening.

- The week sent takes an optional `opening: {take, recordedAt}`, checked as
  an answer's take is (a note id, an instant no later than Send), and held
  by its ref: a held take said for anything but <week>:opening is a 422 on
  `opening.take`. It answers no ticket, so a send of it alone is still
  refused, and a send without it reads and keeps as before.
- The week's record, and the rust index the mailbox pass puts, say
  `opening: {take, recordedAt} | null` from the send that stands.
- An essay (template version 5) may hold `opening`. One that does plays the
  final's opening take, handed to the recorder as takes/opening.<ext> with
  its words, and is refused when the final names none; one without it may
  leave the final's opening take out. Deleting the opening's take withdraws
  the week only when the essay plays it.

No migration: the send is stored as JSON, and an old body has no opening.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
